> Explain what a single-board computer is, in three sentences.
A single-board computer (SBC) is a type of personal computer that contains only a single central processing unit (CPU), memory, and graphics processing unit (GPU). It is designed to be small, lightweight, and portable, making it ideal for use in a variety of applications, from home and office computing to mobile devices and robotics. Single-board computers are known for their portability, ease of use, and ability to expand their processing power by adding additional components such as RAM, storage, and external devices.

